WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:10.670 --> 00:00:11.780
John: 1, 2, 3!

00:00:11.780 --> 00:00:14.300
Crowd: Good morning Hank!

00:00:14.300 --> 00:00:20.340
It's... well, if yesterday was Thursday, and
the day before yesterday was Thursday, then

00:00:20.340 --> 00:00:22.720
today must be... Thursday?

00:00:22.720 --> 00:00:24.630
Crowd: It's Friday!

00:00:24.630 --> 00:00:30.150
Oh, okay, it's Friday, it's Friday, January
26th. Thanks to the George Bruce Branch of

00:00:30.150 --> 00:00:33.370
the New York Public Library for participating.
Let's get right to the survey.

00:00:33.370 --> 00:00:34.890
Puppet: Describe a perfect day.

00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:38.550
John: I wake up in the morning, write four
thousand words, Sarah comes home from school,

00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:42.470
we have a sushi dinner together, and then
we read until it's time to go to bed. Oh,

00:00:42.470 --> 00:00:46.320
and The Office is on, and I watch The Office,
and Pam and Jim hook up. YES!

00:00:46.320 --> 00:00:52.830
Puppet: Assuming... I don't remember the words.
Assuming all things come to an end, how will

00:00:52.830 --> 00:00:53.830
humans go extinct?

00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:56.950
John: Puppet, I'm with T.S. Elliot on this
one; "Not with a bang, but with a whimper."

00:00:56.950 --> 00:00:59.040
Puppet: So how're you feeling about kids these
days?

00:00:59.040 --> 00:01:03.769
John: I really want a baby. But where would
we put one, Hank? Where are we going to fit

00:01:03.769 --> 00:01:07.420
a baby inside this apartment? Are we going
to put it under the bed? I wanna have a baby.

00:01:07.420 --> 00:01:11.659
I wanna have a baby a lot; babies are adorable.
I wanna have like sixteen of 'em, I want to

00:01:11.659 --> 00:01:12.860
have like a little army of babies!

00:01:12.860 --> 00:01:15.680
Puppet: In this space, create your own question
and answer it.

00:01:15.680 --> 00:01:21.310
John: Puppet, the question is, "Pirates or
Ninjas?" Ninjas! I just like how fast they

00:01:21.310 --> 00:01:22.310
strike.

00:01:22.310 --> 00:01:23.920
Puppet: What does ambrosia taste like?

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:26.930
John: You know what ambrosia tastes like?
It tastes like all the things you can't eat

00:01:26.930 --> 00:01:32.880
on Weight Watchers. Cheeseburgers, sugar cookies,
regular freaking ice cream instead of, like,

00:01:32.880 --> 00:01:35.759
ice cream that's made out of air and human
hope.

00:01:35.759 --> 00:01:38.679
Puppet: If you were a cliché, what cliché
would you be?

00:01:38.679 --> 00:01:40.210
John: A dark and stormy night.

00:01:40.210 --> 00:01:42.420
Puppet: What's your least favorite part of
any given day?

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:44.290
John: I don't enjoy brushing my teeth.

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:46.179
Puppet: Do you enjoy science fiction?

00:01:46.179 --> 00:01:50.679
John: I really like Kurt Vonnegut, um, and
I also am a big fan of the short stories of

00:01:50.679 --> 00:01:51.679
Margo Lanagan.

00:01:51.679 --> 00:01:53.110
Puppet: Cheese or chocolate?

00:01:53.110 --> 00:01:57.899
John: Why did you just name two things I can't
eat anymore? God, that's so mean!

00:01:57.899 --> 00:01:59.579
Puppet: What was your first concert?

00:01:59.579 --> 00:02:05.430
John: I think it might have been The Cure,
in 9th grade with Davon Razor. I did like

00:02:05.430 --> 00:02:06.430
The Cure a lot.

00:02:06.430 --> 00:02:07.939
Puppet: Where would you live if you could
live anywhere?

00:02:07.939 --> 00:02:08.980
John: North Carolina.

00:02:08.980 --> 00:02:11.950
Puppet: Would you prefer invisibility or time
travel?

00:02:11.950 --> 00:02:16.280
John: Well, as you can see I already have
the gift of invisibility; I'm wearing my invisibility

00:02:16.280 --> 00:02:18.981
cloak right now, so I guess I would choose
time travel.

00:02:18.981 --> 00:02:22.540
Puppet: If you could start a business that
would be instantly successful, what would

00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:23.540
it be?

00:02:23.540 --> 00:02:28.920
John: A Malaria curing business? A We Only
Sell Novels by John Green Store? Anyway, I'm

00:02:28.920 --> 00:02:33.610
not sure what the store would sell necessarily,
but it would definitely be called The Blind

00:02:33.610 --> 00:02:40.090
Assassin in Your Pants. I'm sorry, I- I can't
stop myself. Thanks to all the commenters

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:41.090
for their great ideas.

00:02:41.090 --> 00:02:47.120
Puppet: What's wrong with the world?

00:02:47.120 --> 00:02:53.710
John: I, I really think the big problem, is,
uh, people. You know, I mean puppets are a

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:57.769
small problem, puppet; I'm, I'm not going
to let you guys off the hook entirely, but,

00:02:57.769 --> 00:02:59.610
but people... we're the worst.

00:02:59.610 --> 00:03:02.090
Puppet: Can I put this survey on my webpage?

00:03:02.090 --> 00:03:04.880
John: You may. Hank, I'll see you on Monday.

